.*
.* WRKUSRJOB and WRKSBSJOB: the jobs of a user or of a subsystem, with
.* the job options of WRKACTJOB.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 7'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 16'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FUNCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=TYPE CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=FUNCTION CLASS=FUNCL.
:VAR NAME=SBS CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SBSLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=JOBS VARS='OPT JOB USER NUMBER TYPE STATUS FUNCTION'.
:KEYL NAME=UJKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display schedule data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=F21 ACTION='RETURN 21'.F21=Select assistance level
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=SJKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display schedule data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKUSRJOB KEYL=UJKEYS HELP=WRKUSRJOB ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with User Jobs
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS MAXHEAD=2.(No jobs to show)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.4=End
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.5=Work with
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPJOBLOG JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.7=Display message
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) OPTION(*SPLF)'.8=Work with spooled files
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD DSCJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.13=Disconnect
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT.Job
:LISTCOL VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT.-----Status-----
:LISTCOL VAR=FUNCTION USAGE=OUTPUT.Function
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSBSJOB KEYL=SJKEYS HELP=WRKSBSJOB ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with Subsystem Jobs
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATAI VAR=SBS USAGE=OUTPUT.Subsystem
.* Not shown: it sets the colon column.
:DATAI VAR=SBSLIB USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Library of subsystem
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=JOBS MAXHEAD=2.(No jobs to show)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.4=End
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.5=Work with
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=7 ENTER='CMD DSPJOBLOG JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.7=Display message
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) OPTION(*SPLF)'.8=Work with spooled files
:LISTACT OPTION=13 ENTER='CMD DSCJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.13=Disconnect
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT.Job
:LISTCOL VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT.-----Status-----
:LISTCOL VAR=FUNCTION USAGE=OUTPUT.Function
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKUSRJOB.Work with User Jobs - Help
:P.The jobs a user profile runs: active ones, ones waiting on a job
queue and ones that ended with spooled output left. Type an option
next to a job, or a command on the command line.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSBSJOB.Work with Subsystem Jobs - Help
:P.The jobs running in a subsystem, or in every active subsystem.
Type an option next to a job, or a command on the command line.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
